"For each cluster, graph the mean square offset (vertical) against the shift (across) and fit a quadratic, \\(a + b\\mu + c\\mu^2\\). Find the shift at the lowest point, \\(\\mu = -b/(2c)\\), and the distance it gives.",
"Press <strong>Cluster A</strong> and <strong>Cluster B</strong> in turn to read each <strong>True distance (simulated)</strong>; for the mystery cluster, use the true distance you wrote down in Part {#}. By how many percent is each of your distances off, and in which direction?",
